   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "3 Sidney St, Lloyds Bank (former Foster's Bank, Alfred Waterhouse): red brick banded with buff stone (horizontal stripes), arcade of round-arched ground-floor windows with stone shafts, gabled dormers/pinnacles on top and the clock tower at the south (p1) corner over a big round-arched stone doorway with a carved pediment (door x~18.6). Tower rising above the eave is not modelled. Bay pitch ~2.6 m estimated from the oblique view 475285070488446 (looking north from the Market St end); x runs north->south."
