   "notes": "Tudor-Gothic ashlar range east of the Lloyds clock tower (Commons geograph 7254731, 2022, CC BY-SA 2.0; right edge of the photo): buff stone, stone-mullioned and transomed leaded windows, a 4-light window on the first floor, a steep coped gable with a 3-light attic window (as dormer), cast-iron downpipe. Only partly in frame, so positions are rough (+-1 m) and the bay count could be off by one."
